WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.640
Let's not kid ourselves: we already all know
that The Last Jedi is going to melt your brain

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.180
when it appears in theaters in December, 2017.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.940
After The Force Awakens revitalized the Star
Wars franchise at the movies in 2015, there

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.320
was little doubt that the follow-up would
probably be pretty amazing.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.760
But now that we've gotten our first real look
at the movie via the debut teaser trailer,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.060
we can say with some certainty that Episode
VIII will take us places we never even knew

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:25.940
we wanted to go.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.520
Here are just a few of the reasons why Star
Wars: The Last Jedi will blow you away in

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.020
December.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.560
Rian Johnson’s sci-fi cred

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.800
When it comes to Hollywood's current crop
of go-to directors, Last Jedi director Rian

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.600
Johnson may not necessarily be a name that
everyone recognizes immediately.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.820
But ask any fan of Johnson, and they'll tell
you he's been helming incredible flicks with

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.940
consistent regularity for years.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:55.100
For example, if you haven't yet checked out
2012's Looper, written and directed by Johnson,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.280
do yourself a favor and make sure you watch
it as soon as possible.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.320
Johnson took a relatively low budget and produced
one of the more memorable and impressive science

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.460
fiction movies in years.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:08.700
Just imagine what he can pull off with the
might of Disney's wallet backing him up.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.480
Lots of Luke

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.340
One of the chief complaints about The Force
Awakens was that Luke Skywalker, the hero

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.400
at the center of the first Star Wars trilogy,
was pretty much absent for the entire movie

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.120
— right up until the very end.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.350
The lack of Luke makes sense in the context
of the film, of course, since finding him

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.310
is one of the movie's main objectives.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:31.040
But some fans couldn't help but be disappointed
that one of the franchise's most important

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.500
characters was barely there.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.380
Now, though, Skywalker's truly back.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:39.870
The new movie seems to have no shortage of
the former farmboy: in this trailer alone,

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:44.909
he presides over some lightsaber training,
hangs out with R2-D2, and even chills near

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:46.060
the mouth of a cave!

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:51.350
In short, fans are going to be up to their
armpits in Luke Skywalker — and that fantastic

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.390
beard of his.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:55.960
If you love Luke — and you obviously do
— your prayers have finally been answered.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.340
Captain Phasma’s return?

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.960
When fans weren't wondering why there wasn't
more Luke in The Force Awakens, they were

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:08.170
probably complaining that Gwendoline Christie
was painfully underused as the shiniest stormtrooper

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.840
of them all, Captain Phasma.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.960
She yelled at Finn, talked to her boss that
one time, then got dumped into a trash compactor.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.200
"Aghh!"

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.620
Would that really be all we got of the Captain?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.440
As it turns out, no, it wouldn't.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.900
We only see her for a moment in the new trailer,
but unless the First Order has started handing

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.700
out shiny stormtrooper outfits to anyone who
asks, that's Phasma.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:36.440
What she's doing in The Last Jedi is, of course,
totally unknown, but it's good to know she's back.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.700
Rey of light...or dark

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.920
In a revelation that should surprise exactly
no one, The Last Jedi will finally start to

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.130
answer some of the questions about Rey that
fans have been asking since she first showed

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.140
up in The Force Awakens.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:55.320
Speaking during the 2017 installment of Star
Wars Celebration, actress Daisy Ridley said,

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:59.840
simply, "What I can say is, in The Last Jedi,
we go deeper into Rey's story."

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.380
It was always a given that the hints of Rey's
origins and destiny we saw in the previous

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.620
movie would get more exploration in the follow-up.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.880
Now that she's been training with Luke Skywalker,
she may make some discoveries about herself

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.800
and where she really came from that could
shock her — and fans — to the core.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.120
Speaking of which...

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.140
Shades of Empire Strikes Back

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.040
It's an oft-repeated truism, but you can never
say it too many times: The Empire Strikes

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.840
Back is the best installment in the Star Wars
saga.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.060
So it's exciting to see that The Last Jedi
seems to be going in a similar direction.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.240
Need proof?

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.780
There's a moment in the new trailer where
a bunch of ships are speeding toward a confrontation

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:40.160
with a marching battalion of walkers — just
like what happened on Hoth during the first

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.460
act of Empire Strikes Back.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.379
Then there's the serious struggle our heroes
will have to endure and overcome, another

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.300
hallmark of Empire.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.940
Take, for instance, the scene where Poe Dameron
and BB-8 are racing towards their X-Wing,

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.300
only to recoil from an explosion.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.340
Now, remember how Luke got his X-Wing stuck
in the mud on Dagobah?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.120
Or how the Millennium Falcon's hyperdrive
just kept malfunctioning?

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.860
We only have the barest threads of The Last
Jedi's plot to speculate with, but it seems

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:10.860
like this new movie aims to echo many fans'
favorite Star Wars movie in plenty of ways.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.920
Hello, Rose

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.780
While Rey is sequestered away as Luke's student,
Finn and Poe will need another ally.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.760
While she doesn't seem to appear in the trailer,
Rose will be the new character to take on

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:22.260
that role.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:27.660
Variety reports that actress Kelly Marie Tran
will appear in The Last Jedi as a maintenance

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:32.660
worker in the Resistance who joins Finn as
he gets into his latest round of galactic hijinks.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:38.120
Outside of that, we don't know a whole lot
about Rose, though Johnson did say this at

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.200
Star Wars Celebration:

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.040
"She’s not a soldier [...] She’s not looking
to be a hero, and she gets pulled a very big

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.480
way into an adventure in this movie with Finn
[John Boyega]."

00:04:46.949 --> 00:04:51.300
As to what else we can expect from Rose in
The Last Jedi, it's way too soon to tell.

00:04:51.309 --> 00:04:54.880
But it's pretty exciting to know that there's
a whole new major character coming that didn't

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.120
even make it into the trailer.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.920
Imagine what other surprises and twists were
left out...

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.020
Farewell, Princess

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.120
Despite the excitement that comes with a new
Star Wars movie, it's hard to forget that

00:05:05.139 --> 00:05:09.849
actress Carrie Fisher passed away in late
2016, leaving a hole at the very heart of

00:05:09.849 --> 00:05:10.560
the saga itself.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.570
We know that Fisher finished filming her scenes
for Episode VIII before she died, and we catch

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.719
a glimpse of Leia in the new trailer as well.

00:05:17.719 --> 00:05:22.229
Chances seem good that The Last Jedi will
provide a fitting farewell for her, giving

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:27.220
grieving fans some closure on one of cinema's
most iconic characters, and one of Hollywood's

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.240
most beloved actresses.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.040
Delivering on the title’s promise

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:36.479
Towards the end of the trailer, Luke offers
a cryptic confession, saying he only knows

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.160
one truth:

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:41.260
"It's time for the Jedi to end."

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.659
While fans have been speculating about the
movie title's significance since it was first

00:05:45.659 --> 00:05:50.889
announced, the trailer seems to be giving
us a definitive idea about what it'll mean.

00:05:50.889 --> 00:05:54.360
The Jedi as we've known them aren't going
to be reborn with Rey.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.240
Rather, their time is coming to an end.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:00.831
It's also important to keep in mind that not
everyone who practiced the Light side of the

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.240
Force was a Jedi, as little Maz Kanata can
attest.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:10.220
And let's also not forget that the Jedi weren't
necessarily, like, super awesome, you know?

00:06:10.229 --> 00:06:16.060
The Jedi Council's shortsightedness and rigidity
helped turn Anakin Skywalker into Darth Vader,

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.849
while allowing the Emperor to take over the
Republic.

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:23.069
And Luke's attempts to start a new bunch of
Jedi led to Ben Solo turning his back on his

00:06:23.069 --> 00:06:24.930
family and becoming Kylo Ren.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.360
Suffice it to say, the end of the Jedi might
not be such a bad thing…

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.620
"Here's some money, go see a Star War."

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.300
Thanks for watching!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.880
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:37.289 --> 00:06:39.920
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love too.

